You have a React Native repository and no CI/CD configuration. Start here, then follow the pages in order. Android and iOS instructions appear where their build, signing, and delivery steps differ.

**This page:** identify your source repository, obtain the required access, and choose the next setup step.

**By the end of this section:** a reviewed source revision produces tested, signed packages and reaches its approved destination, with the exact version and intended audience verified.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Keep credentials, signing files, private binaries, and sensitive logs in approved systems. Redact screenshots before adding them here.

## 1. Understand what you are setting up

**Continuous integration (CI)** checks changes automatically: code review rules, tests, coverage, and compilation. **Continuous delivery (CD)** prepares and delivers an approved version. Public store release still requires its applicable approvals.

| Tool | What it does for your app |
| :--- | :--- |
| Git repository | Stores the application, configuration, and reviewed tests. A commit identifies a specific source revision. |
| Bitrise | Runs the configured checks, builds Android/iOS binaries, and executes delivery steps. |
| CAMP (`campfile.yml`) | Records application identity and Enterprise metadata in the application repository. |
| Danger.js | Adds automated pull request feedback using the team's review rules. |
| Sauce Labs | Runs the committed device tests on physical Android and iOS devices and provides test evidence. |
| NowSecure | Assesses the built application for security findings; the configured severity gate controls progression. |
| App Management / stores | Makes approved versions available to their intended users or testers. |

A **pull request (PR)** asks reviewers to approve a proposed change. A **binary** is the packaged app: Android APK/AAB or iOS IPA. An Android App Bundle (`.aab`) is used for Google Play delivery; it is not an APK to install directly.

A **workflow** is an ordered build job. A **pipeline** coordinates jobs. **GitOps enrollment** means submitting a reviewed YAML request so platform automation can create and configure the Bitrise app.

