**GitOps** means requesting platform configuration through a reviewed Git change. You submit YAML; authorized automation creates and connects the Bitrise app.

**Starting point:** the application source is published, the preparation page is complete, and Platform Engineering has supplied the configuration repository, approved template/version, and access group.

**Outcome:** submit one reviewed request, track its protected apply run, and verify the resulting Bitrise app identity. Enrollment success is separate from build or delivery success.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Enrollment YAML contains application metadata, never credentials or credential references.

Use this page for a **new enrollment**. If the application already exists, ask Platform Engineering to confirm its identity and continue with its existing configuration. Do not submit another create request.

## 1. Confirm the two repositories

| Repository | Contains | Branch used here |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Application repository | Mobile source, tests, and `campfile.yml`. | Actual source branch required by the approved template. |
| Central configuration repository | Enrollment request and approved catalog/process. | Request branch → `develop` → protected `main`. |

Complete [Repository Preparation](../repository-readiness/) first. Obtain the approved template ID/version and access group from Platform Engineering. Record the application repository, branch, and published commit separately from the configuration revision.

Use the supplied Build & Release Kit/workshop GitOps process. The handbook's underlying console setup is platform-owned; developers do not also create the app manually.

## 2. Create a request branch

**Where:** a local checkout of the central configuration repository, not your React Native checkout.

Inspect the checkout first:

```bash
git status --short --branch
git remote get-url origin
```

Confirm the correct remote and a clean working tree. Commit or otherwise preserve unrelated work using your team's process before switching branches.

The following commands assume local `develop` already exists and `origin` points to the approved configuration repository:

```bash
git fetch origin &&
  git switch develop &&
  git merge --ff-only origin/develop &&
  git switch -c feature/enroll-sample-mobile
```

Replace `sample-mobile` with the intended app name. The request branch pattern comes from the Build & Release Kit. If `develop` is missing, the branch already exists, or fast-forward fails, resolve the checkout with the repository maintainer; do not force-reset it.

**Expected:** you are on your request branch, based on the current configuration `develop` branch.

## 3. Create the enrollment YAML

**File:** `config/teams/<team>/bitrise/apps/<app_name>.yaml`.

