| Caching and parallelism | Cache approved downloads and parallelize independent jobs within account capacity. |
| Versioning and disk | Keep approved pins; remove only known temporary outputs under the owning workflow's policy. |
| Bad practices | No plaintext secrets, bypassed failures, unnecessary full builds, missing cache setup, or unstructured all-purpose release job. |

Use Linux or an approved compatible runner for Android and macOS/Xcode for iOS. Confirm the selected stack/toolchain matches the repository.

The SOT's cost figures—approximately 1 credit/minute for standard Linux, 2–4 for macOS, 30–50 credits per example build, and $14.49 per 100 credits—are **source illustrations, not verified Enterprise billing rates**. Use the actual account's machine rates, duration, concurrency, and contracted limits before estimating cost. Do not promise a fixed saving from parallel execution.

