## 2. Add Danger to the approved review-tooling project

**Where:** the trusted checkout selected by Platform Engineering. The root `dangerfile.ts` must be reviewed before running it with the bot credential. Do not load a PR author's edited rules or dependency lifecycle scripts into that protected context.

The SOT supplies either of these installation commands:

```bash
# Yarn project: use this option.
yarn add danger --dev
```

```bash
# npm project: use this alternative.
npm install danger --save-dev
```

Run only the command matching the approved project package manager. Use its approved dependency-version policy and review the resulting manifest/lockfile; a new install must not silently upgrade governed tooling. These are developer setup instructions, not commands executed while preparing this documentation.

**Expected:** the trusted tooling has a locally resolved Danger dependency and committed lockfile.

## 3. Create `dangerfile.ts`

**File:** `dangerfile.ts` at the root of the approved trusted review-tooling checkout. Copy the source rules below, then append the mandatory-control block in this section to that same file. Do not create two separate Dangerfiles or duplicate the import.

The following is the latest SOT's rule script, retained as supplied:

```typescript
import { danger, warn, fail, message } from "danger";

// Check if PR has a description
const prDescription = danger.github.pr.body;
if (!prDescription || prDescription.length < 10) {
  warn("Please provide a detailed description for your Pull Request.");
}

// Check if PR has assignees
if (danger.github.pr.assignee === null) {
  warn("Please assign someone to this PR.");
}

// Check PR size
const modifiedFiles = danger.git.modified_files.length;
const createdFiles = danger.git.created_files.length;
const totalChanges = modifiedFiles + createdFiles;

if (totalChanges > 20) {
  warn(`This PR has ${totalChanges} changed files. Consider breaking it down into smaller PRs.`);
}

message(`Changed files in this PR: ${totalChanges}`);
```

| Rule | Exact behavior of this script |
| :--- | :--- |
| Missing body or fewer than 10 characters | Warning. It counts raw characters, not trimmed meaningful content. |
| `assignee === null` | Warning. |
| More than 20 created + modified files | Warning. Deleted files are not counted by this source implementation. |
| Total changed-file message | Informational comment. |

Although `fail` is imported, the source script never calls it. It does **not** enforce the earlier mandatory description/assignee/reviewer/draft rules by itself. Add the blocking extension below or retain equivalent approved trusted controls. Two peer approvals remain governed by the repository policy; a Danger comment is not an approval.

If the approved mandatory rules are implemented in this same file, a blocking rule must call `fail(...)`, not merely `warn(...)`. Do not replace the source warning thresholds or silently weaken the existing rules. [Danger feedback reference](https://danger.systems/js/reference).

### Retain the earlier mandatory PR controls

Append this explicit integration of the earlier supplied mandatory rules after the source warning script, in the **same trusted `dangerfile.ts`**. It adds blocking description, assignee, designated-reviewer, and draft/WIP checks; it leaves the latest SOT's warning rules intact.

```typescript
// Earlier mandatory controls, added alongside the latest SOT warning rules.
const pr = danger.github.pr;
if ((pr.body ?? "").trim().length < 10) {
  fail("Provide a meaningful PR description of at least 10 characters.");
}
if ((pr.assignees?.length ?? (pr.assignee ? 1 : 0)) === 0) {
  fail("Assign the PR to its responsible owner.");
}
const draft: unknown = "draft" in pr ? pr.draft : undefined;
if (typeof draft !== "boolean") {
  fail("Draft status is unavailable; the required PR check cannot pass.");
} else if (draft || /\[wip\]|\(wip\)|^\s*wip\b/i.test(pr.title)) {
  fail("Complete draft/WIP work before merge.");
}
const requested = danger.github.requested_reviewers;
const designated = requested.users.some(user => user.login !== pr.user.login) ||
  requested.teams.length > 0 ||
  danger.github.reviews.some(review =>
    review.user.login !== pr.user.login && review.user.type !== "Bot");
if (!designated) {
  fail("Designate the required reviewer or team.");
}
```

This checks reviewer designation, not approval count, reviewer eligibility, unresolved change requests, or stale reviews. Repository protection must enforce the supplied two-peer approval policy. Verify these metadata fields against the pinned Danger/GitHub Enterprise integration; unavailable metadata must fail the required status rather than being treated as approved.

