The source does not supply the custom check's assessment-ID linkage, completion polling, outputs, or timeout contract. Confirm that it selects the completed assessment of the **exact candidate**, rather than an older scan of the same package. Package name alone is insufficient. Do not invent an assessment-ID input.

## 10. Verify the security decision and notifications

Inspect the completed assessment and build result. Record source commit, route, artifact hash, assessment reference, evaluated policy, and the actual failing/passing step.

| Result | Required action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Critical/High finding | Block delivery and route the finding to its remediation owner. |
| Medium finding | Apply the confirmed policy; the supplied custom example blocks at Medium. |
| Assessment pending, unavailable, or timed out | Keep progression blocked until a conclusive approved result exists. |
| Clean completed assessment | Continue only when all other required gates and approvals also pass. |
| Notification or issue created | Verify its recipient/repository and sanitized content. This is not proof the vulnerability is fixed. |

The source describes email alerts, GitHub issue creation, and a non-zero build exit on threshold breach. Verify each against a controlled approved test or existing evidence; do not deliberately introduce a vulnerability into a release candidate to test the gate.

