**Code signing** adds a cryptographic signature to the app. Before delivery, verify that the package uses the identity approved for its destination.

**Starting point:** your repository is enrolled in Bitrise and its approved build workflow is available.

**Result:** verify the signed package produced by the existing approved workflow, then pass it to delivery.

**Configuration scope:** SOT requirements remain authoritative. The standard Bitrise examples and verification commands added below are explicitly identified as vendor-backed additions. Platform Engineering supplies the approved versions, route values, and protected credential bindings before use.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Never put passwords, private keys, certificates with private keys, or signing files in Git or screenshots.

