## 4. Record all seven release-evidence milestones


| Milestone | Evidence |
| :--- | :--- |
| `BuildStarted` | Actual source commit/branch, route, workflow, template and inputs. |
| `BuildSuccessful` | Identified configured build completed successfully. |
| `ArtifactValidated` | Non-zero package, correct type/identity, hash and gate associations. |
| `Uploaded` | Authoritative destination receipt/version identity. |
| `Signed` | Required native/downstream signature and expected identity. |
| `Enabled` | Destination-specific required active/available state. |
| `Assigned & UserVisible` | Approved audience and exact-version visibility through the intended user's endpoint. |

These are evidence categories, not universal chronological signing order. Installation/launch is separate if acceptance requires it. An uploaded object awaiting signing/enablement is a **Provisional Upload Checkpoint**, never a completed release. Missing assignment/visibility also leaves delivery incomplete.

**Example evidence record — documentation-owned, not an API schema:**

```yaml
source_commit: REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_COMMIT
route: qa_android
template: { id: APPROVED_ID, version: APPROVED_VERSION }
build_ref: INTERNAL_BUILD_REFERENCE
artifact:
  type: apk
  sha256: REPLACE_WITH_OBSERVED_HASH
  size_bytes: 0 # Replace with observed positive size.
destination:
  version_ref: INTERNAL_VERSION_REFERENCE
  audience_ref: APPROVED_AUDIENCE_REFERENCE
milestones:
  BuildStarted: unknown
  BuildSuccessful: unknown
  ArtifactValidated: unknown
  Uploaded: unknown
  Signed: unknown
  Enabled: unknown
  "Assigned & UserVisible": unknown
evidence_ref: INTERNAL_VERIFICATION_RECORD
```

Replace unknowns only with supported actual results/references in the approved evidence system. Do not add private download URLs. Never default all apps to All Users; apply intended business entitlements.


## 5. Continue later builds without reenrollment

The supplied Build & Release Kit describes recurring distribution of eligible successful builds using the enrolled app identity and a **durable milestone cursor**: a persisted record of completed work for that candidate/route.

After a worker restart or uncertain write, Platform Engineering reconciles actual destination state before any remaining authorized action. Do not replay enrollment, reset progress, duplicate an upload, or infer absence from a single inconclusive read. The actual cursor/storage/concurrency contract is platform-owned and was not supplied as copy-ready code.

## 6. Record each route independently

| Route | Build | Signing | Destination version / audience | Outcome |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `qa_android` | Observed result/reference | Observed result/reference | Verified evidence/reference | Actual result |
| `qa_ios` | Observed result/reference | Observed result/reference | Verified evidence/reference | Actual result |
| `uat_android` | Observed result/reference | Observed result/reference | Verified evidence/reference | Actual result |
| `uat_ios` | Observed result/reference | Observed result/reference | Verified evidence/reference | Actual result |

Use the actual platform status vocabulary; do not turn pending, not-started, or unknown work into success. The historical workshop confirmed QA Android delivery, failed QA iOS downstream signing, and did not confirm UAT publication: overall **partial failure**.

## If delivery fails

| Result | Next action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Local package missing or wrong identity | Fix the candidate handoff before any upload. |
| Destination rejects authentication | Have the integration owner inspect credential binding and permissions. |
| Version/build is already present | Reconcile its source/candidate identity; do not blindly re-upload or alter version numbers to evade the error. |
| Upload accepted but processing is pending | Monitor that same candidate/version; do not submit it again. |
| Signing, enablement, or audience assignment fails | Preserve the existing destination object and inspect the failed operation. |
| Timeout with unknown create/upload outcome | Stop writes and request approved read-only reconciliation. |
| Version not visible to intended users | Verify destination/version, processing, assignment, eligibility, and access; do not call delivery complete. |

