import { Tabs, TabItem } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import MermaidZoom from '../components/mermaid-zoom.astro';

**Starting point:** a validation, build, test, scan, signing, or delivery operation failed or has an unknown result.

**Outcome:** identify the failed boundary, preserve completed work, and either fix a local issue or obtain an owner-approved recovery decision.

> **Confidential — Enterprise internal use only.** Share sanitized errors and references, not raw logs, tokens, signing files, or private download URLs.

## 1. Open the exact failed run

In Bitrise, open the failed build and identify the first failed step. For enrollment failures, ask the authorized Vela operator for the apply/preview result matching the configuration revision.

Record the run reference, actual source commit, workflow/route, configuration revision, template version, failed step, and error. Check earlier steps for completed uploads, registrations, or signing operations.

| What failed? | First action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Local/schema/lint/test/compile check before external writes | Fix the reported source/configuration issue and rerun its relevant checks. |
| External create/upload/sign/distribute operation | Inspect actual destination state before deciding on another action. |
| Timeout, lost response, or interrupted external operation | Treat the result as unknown; stop writes and request reconciliation. |
| One route failed after another succeeded | Preserve the successful route and investigate the failed route separately. |
| Destination is still processing | Monitor that same candidate; do not upload it again to accelerate processing. |

**Expected:** you know which operation failed and whether external effects may already exist. A red build does not mean nothing happened.

**Attach screenshot — failed step and source/run identity, with sensitive values redacted.**

## 2. Apply the SOT one-write rule

An external mutation creates or changes something: an app, upload, test job, signed version, assignment, or release. Under the supplied rule, do not blindly repeat an uncertain mutation.

<MermaidZoom title="Classify the failure before performing another external action">

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Failed step or missing response"] --> B{"Could an external write have occurred?"}
    B -->|No| C["Correct local source/configuration"]
    C --> D["Rerun relevant checks"]
    B -->|Yes or unknown| E["Stop writes and preserve state"]
    E --> F["Owner performs read-only reconciliation"]
    F --> G{"Actual result confirmed?"}
    G -->|Completed| H["Reuse confirmed result"]
    G -->|Pending or unknown| I["Observe within approved limits or escalate"]
    G -->|Failure or absence established| J["Owner reviews remaining recovery action"]
    classDef inspect fill:#172554,stroke:#93c5fd,color:#fff,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef stop fill:#881337,stroke:#fda4af,color:#fff,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef owner fill:#4c1d95,stroke:#d8b4fe,color:#fff,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef done fill:#064e3b,stroke:#6ee7b7,color:#fff,stroke-width:2px;
    class A,B,G inspect;
    class E,I stop;
    class F,J owner;
    class C,D,H done;
```

</MermaidZoom>

The Sauce source claims automatic API backoff at 2/4/8 seconds. That is not authorization to retry an uncertain registration, upload, or job submission. Platform owners must inspect the pinned implementation's retry behavior against the one-write rule. Read retries and conclusively unsent requests require their actual adapter contract; this guide supplies no generic mutation retry loop.

## 3. Collect local evidence without changing remote state

**Where:** the relevant application or configuration checkout. These commands are documentation diagnostic aids:

```bash
git status --short --branch
git rev-parse --show-toplevel
git branch --show-current
git rev-parse HEAD
```

For a known existing candidate, run this block as Bash in its approved environment:

```bash
set -euo pipefail

MOBILE_EXISTING_ARTIFACT='/REPLACE/path/to/existing-candidate'
test -s "$MOBILE_EXISTING_ARTIFACT"
shasum -a 256 "$MOBILE_EXISTING_ARTIFACT"
```

