## 4. Diagnose the reported error

| Symptom | Inspect / next action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Enrollment YAML rejected | Match team directory and filename to `team`/`app_name`; check allowed fields, exact template version, branch, and forbidden secrets/mutation fields. Rerun validation on the updated PR revision. |
| CAMP rejected | Use the latest flat schema supported by the consumer. Resolve initial Bitrise/dashboard fields with the owner; do not combine nested/flat formats or submit fabricated URLs. |
| Vela preview absent or stale | Match current PR head to its check run. Have the authorized operator inspect the actual pending/error result over the approved access path. |
| Repository/registry access denied | Have the owner check the bound integration's permissions and exact source/ref. Do not embed a personal token in the clone URL or bypass TLS. |
| Danger missing or failing | Inspect PR event/mapping, trusted tooling/dependency, bot binding, current metadata, and required status. Fix the actual failure without weakening mandatory rules. |
| Danger only warns | The original SOT script is warning-only. Confirm the earlier mandatory blocking extension/approved equivalent and branch protection are active. |
| Module tests all skipped | Inspect producer/downstream flags and event comparison. Missing/empty comparisons must select all modules; missing/invalid worker metadata must fail. |
| Tests pass with no useful evidence | Verify test discovery, filters, expected suites, source scope, coverage thresholds, and actual reports. Missing required tests are not success. |
| Android signing fails | Inspect exact input/output, key alias/password binding, and expected certificate. A remote keystore URL is not a local Gradle file path. |
| iOS archive/export fails | Inspect first Xcode error, scheme, identifiers/extensions, team, profiles/private key, entitlements, distribution method, and exact step input contract. |
| Exit 137 | Inspect timeout/memory/runner evidence. The exit code alone does not establish a specific cause or universal timeout. |
| `ENOSPC` | Inspect disk evidence and selected stack quota; owner reviews cleanup of operation-owned outputs. |
| Store rejects version/build | Confirm package/bundle, submitted version/build, existing destination state, and actual acceptance. Reconcile before changing numbers or resubmitting. |
| Store upload succeeds but version is unavailable | Check processing, release/track state, compliance/review, tester group/eligibility, and exact build assignment. |
| Private version is invisible | Check destination environment, signing/enablement, audience/entitlements, and exact-version visibility. Do not assign everyone as a workaround. |

## 5. Inspect Sauce Labs and NowSecure failures

The following maps the supplied integration errors to an investigation. Exact private step behavior still follows its approved contract.

| Source symptom | Evidence and next action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Missing Sauce credentials / HTTP 401 | Owner checks `SAUCE_USERNAME` / `SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY`, account access, and region. Never paste values into a report. |
| Missing `saucelabs.request.yml` / schema error | Confirm committed root file and schema expected by the pinned custom step. Source editions differ; do not guess input aliases. |
| App already exists | Reconcile app/storage identity with the request and candidate. The source suggests renaming; do not use a new name to evade an uncertain prior create under governed recovery. |
| Binary missing | Confirm upstream build, supported package form, actual output variable, and file transfer between runners. |
| Upload present but registration appears empty | Match app/file/storage ID, actual bytes, region, and source receipt before any further write. |
| HTTP 404 / wrong region | Check identity, region, permissions, filters/pagination, and processing. One not-found response does not prove absence. |
| Device allocation timeout | Inspect available matrix/capacity and existing job state. A queued run is not a test pass; do not blindly submit a second job. |
| Test command exits non-zero | Inspect suite discovery, framework configuration, device logs/video, and failed assertions. Preserve the original exit result. |
| NowSecure assessment pending | Track that exact assessment/candidate; submission accepted is not completion. |
| NowSecure blocks findings | Apply confirmed policy. Source examples differ at High versus Medium; do not lower a threshold to pass. |
| Security alerts/issues absent after failure | Inspect failure-path reporting. A failed assessment step may prevent a normal later notification step from running. |

The source's automatic masking claim is not proof all logs are safe to share. Review/redact logs, screenshots, videos, report URLs, and user data before retention or escalation.

## 6. Have the owner reconcile external state

**Developer:** supply the execution, application/version, route, hash, and correlation references already available.

**Authorized owner:** use the actual service's documented GET/read-only adapter to match the operation to its existing destination result. No internal readback endpoints or credential contracts were supplied, so this guide does not invent cURL commands.

| Readback result | Decision |
| :--- | :--- |
| Correct existing result confirmed | Preserve and reuse/reconcile it. Do not recreate or upload it again. |
| Pending/inconclusive | Continue bounded observation or escalate under the approved procedure. |
| Not found once | Check environment, permissions, region, filters, pagination, and eventual consistency. |
| Failure/absence conclusively established | Owner decides the permitted remaining action under the actual recovery contract. Absence alone is not automatic replay authorization. |

Do not reenroll, replay a protected merge, delete/recreate resources, reset milestone cursors, or replace signing material as an assumed fix. If an authorized recovery action itself has an uncertain result, stop again and reconcile it.

## 7. Preserve successful routes

| Workshop evidence | Correct response |
| :--- | :--- |
| QA Android signed, enabled, assigned, and user-visible. | Preserve that confirmed delivery. |
| QA iOS build passed; downstream `distribution_signing_failed`. | Investigate QA iOS destination signing separately. Do not infer a certificate root cause. |
| UAT publication unconfirmed. | Record it as unconfirmed, not successful. |

The reference execution was a partial failure. Acceptance as a known workshop issue did not establish a production fix.

## 8. Send a short support record

Use the approved Teams support channel. Replace these fields with sanitized references; this is a documentation aid, not an API schema:

```text
App / environment / route:
Actual source commit / configuration merge / template version:
Build or Vela run reference / correlation ID:
Failed operation and sanitized error:
Candidate hash / destination version reference:
Confirmed successful operations/routes:
Read-only reconciliation result:
Still pending or unknown:
Requested platform/security/store-owner decision:
```

Sending a support message does not authorize another mutation. Credential/data exposure follows the Enterprise incident process. Apply any approved fix to the correct source/configuration and verify the resulting candidate through its required gates.

