## 6. Invoke the native runner after verified upload

**File:** `scripts/testing/run-native-sauce.sh`. This documentation-owned wrapper runs **inside the approved Bitrise job**, after the adapter has established the matching remote app/test references.

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
set +x
: "${SAUCE_USERNAME:?Protected Sauce identity required}"
: "${SAUCE_ACCESS_KEY:?Protected Sauce access key required}"
: "${MOBILE_NATIVE_FRAMEWORK:?espresso or xcuitest required}"
: "${MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF:?Verified current app storage reference required}"
: "${MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF:?Verified matching test runner storage reference required}"
: "${MOBILE_SAUCE_REGION:?Approved Sauce region required}"
: "${MOBILE_TEST_BUILD_LABEL:?Sanitized build correlation label required}"
for reference in "$MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF" "$MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF"; do
  case "$reference" in
    storage:*) [[ -n "${reference#storage:}" ]] || exit 1 ;;
    *) exit 1 ;;
  esac
done
[[ "$MOBILE_NATIVE_APP_REF" != "$MOBILE_NATIVE_TEST_REF" ]] || exit 1
case "$MOBILE_NATIVE_FRAMEWORK" in
  espresso)
    : "${MOBILE_ANDROID_OS:?Approved Android OS target required}"
    config='.sauce/espresso.yml'
    ;;
  xcuitest)
    : "${MOBILE_IOS_OS:?Approved iOS OS target required}"
    config='.sauce/xcuitest.yml'
    ;;
  *) exit 1 ;;
esac
test -s "$config"
command -v saucectl >/dev/null
exec saucectl run --config "$config"
```

