## 10. Diagnose failures safely

| Source symptom | Inspect / next action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Missing credentials / HTTP 401 | Owner checks protected bindings, account access, and region. Never print or automatically rotate keys. |
| Missing request / schema validation | Confirm root/working directory and the exact schema for the pinned custom step. |
| App already exists | Reconcile identity and existing state; do not choose a new name to evade an uncertain create. |
| Binary missing / unsupported type | Check upstream producer, actual output path, platform/framework package form, and transfer. |
| Upload succeeds but empty registration | Match actual storage receipt, app/file identity, bytes, and region before another write. |
| HTTP 404 / wrong region | Inspect ID, access, region, filters/pagination, and processing; one miss does not prove absence. |
| Allocation timeout | Inspect approved pool/matrix/capacity; record infrastructure failure, not an assertion pass. |
| No tests / wrong filter | Inspect packaged runner/class and selector; reject empty required suites. |
| Chicken-order UI assertion fails | Inspect initial fixture, real selectors, total format, synchronization, and actual receipt; no fixed sleeps or real-order retries. |
| Sauce fails but Bitrise passes | Inspect custom-step/wrapper exit handling and required status. Do not disable failure propagation. |
| Timeout after upload/job submission | Stop writes and reconcile storage/job state before any repeat. |

The source's 2/4/8-second automatic retry and masking claims are unverified private-step behavior. They do not override the one-write rule or establish that logs are safe to share. Preserve the original failure and inspect actual implementation behavior before making this integration a release gate.

